Dame Quay is a [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] Pactbroker and Argyle's contact within the organization. She answers his calls at a private line and keeps the file on his work, and she has offered to send an information packet to his residence when there is anything to report.

When Argyle reported the two [[Ugathal]] that ambushed the party in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], she said she would ask members of the [[Org/The Scale/index|Everchain]] whether they had seen their like before. She is blunt and hard to satisfy; when Argyle called the members of his new group friendly, she answered that he seemed friendly too, and she would still call him dangerous.

By the time Argyle came back she had moved to a guarded office and was not wearing a raiment; she is folded out of paper, greyish-yellow, her face and arms unfolding and folding again as she flips through a folder. She told Argyle he had gotten himself into something this time, said she did not want to send him back out immediately, and still called him dangerous. She keeps her own supervisor, who is busy, and her records showed that Argyle had faxed something from a Pactbroker station in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] with the Party present. She said if anything bearing his number reached her, it was him.

She briefed him in a smoke-filled room beside the goat-legged fiend he calls [[Divinity/Fiends/Flintlock Toboggan|Flintlock]], who wore suit trousers cut below the knee and a vest over burn-scarred skin.
